From 80987bb2bad3a9ace3b36eda28b3b78559d847e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dave Seddon <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:54:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH iproute2] iplink_bond_slave: read ad_partner_oper_port_state
 as u16
To: netdev@vger.kernel.org
Cc: Stephen Hemminger <stephen@networkplumber.org>,
    David Ahern <dsahern@kernel.org>,
    Jay Vosburgh <jv@jvosburgh.net>,
    Hangbin Liu <liuhangbin@gmail.com>

The kernel sends IFLA_BOND_SLAVE_AD_PARTNER_OPER_PORT_STATE as u16:
nla_put_u16() in bond_fill_slave_info(), bond_netlink.c, from
struct port_params.port_state, which is u16. iproute2 reads it with
rta_getattr_u8(), which returns only the first payload byte.

On little endian that is the low byte, and the output is right because
the partner state never exceeds 0xff. On big endian it is the high
byte, which is always zero, so every bond port prints:

    ad_partner_oper_port_state 0 ad_partner_oper_port_state_str <>

Reproduced on s390x under qemu-user by replaying a generated
RTM_NEWLINK message: partner state 0x3f prints 0 before this change and
63 after.

The code used rta_getattr_u16() until commit 39ac2d2b802b ("iplink:
bond: print lacp actor/partner oper states as strings") copied the
actor (u8) block for the partner.

Fixes: 39ac2d2b802b ("iplink: bond: print lacp actor/partner oper states as strings")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dave Seddon <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
---
Found while using an LLM to help port iproute2's netlink handling to
Go. The LLM spotted the mismatch and drafted this patch; I tested it
and can answer for it.

I also have a testsuite test for this (generated bond slave messages
decoded with "ip -d monitor file", red without this patch and green
with it, on x86_64 and on s390x) plus a fix to lib/generic.sh
test_on_not that the test needs. Happy to send them if wanted.

 ip/iplink_bond_slave.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ip/iplink_bond_slave.c b/ip/iplink_bond_slave.c
index f4b28fbc..24e73575 100644
--- a/ip/iplink_bond_slave.c
+++ b/ip/iplink_bond_slave.c
@@ -145,7 +145,7 @@ static void bond_slave_print_opt(struct link_util *lu, FILE *f, struct rtattr *t
 	}
 
 	if (tb[IFLA_BOND_SLAVE_AD_PARTNER_OPER_PORT_STATE]) {
-		__u16 state = rta_getattr_u8(tb[IFLA_BOND_SLAVE_AD_PARTNER_OPER_PORT_STATE]);
+		__u16 state = rta_getattr_u16(tb[IFLA_BOND_SLAVE_AD_PARTNER_OPER_PORT_STATE]);
 
 		print_int(PRINT_ANY,
 			  "ad_partner_oper_port_state",
-- 
